1
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:03,050
He’s a serial killer.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:04,700
We’ll take him in dead or alive.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:11,600
Asura gave me the right
to decide the ending.

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:16,480
Which means I, as the creator,
am the only person who knows the password.

5
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,200
I have a video.

6
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,490
I’ll take them down.

7
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,330
I don’t care
which big shot is behind this.

8
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:26,200
Release? How?

9
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,950
The evidence is obviously against him.

10
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:29,800
I think something is getting fishy.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,770
You should contact Nop right away.

12
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,100
Inspector.

13
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:57,370
We’ve found that the victim’s wallet,
gun, and all valuables are gone.

14
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:00,240
I suspect it is a robbery gone wrong.

15
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:19,100
I’ll think about
Asura’s password on my own.

16
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:20,500
You should rest.

17
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:23,600
It’s okay.

18
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:25,300
I’m fine.

19
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:27,000
Phat.

20
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,800
You’re allowed to be weak.

21
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:35,800
You don’t have to carry everything
on your own.

22
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:47,900
Oh, Inspector.

23
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:48,900
Good timing, sir.

24
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,300
Hang on a minute.

25
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,800
You have a parcel.

26
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:55,900
Here.

27
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,400
Thank you.

28
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,610
NOPPHAN KONGKRAM

29
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:02,900
Nop.

30
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,680
How was it? Everything okay?

31
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:54,490
DSI has examined the evidence.

32
00:02:54,870 --> 00:02:56,300
They took the case.

33
00:02:57,050 --> 00:02:59,360
Kitti won’t get away with it this time.

34
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:10,100
(Praew has been discharged.)

35
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:12,900
Thank you.

36
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:17,610
The doctor said Praew can come home now.

37
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,800
I’ll go to the hospital with you.

38
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,600
Let’s go.

39
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,200
He’s waiting for you, sir.

40
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,300
I’m sorry, sir.

41
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,020
I’ve made a mess.

42
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:51,400
But your nephew was partly to blame.

43
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:58,100
I know my nephew well.

44
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:02,400
I’m not evading responsibility
by blaming anyone.

45
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,250
I’m just saying
we all play a part in this.

46
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:07,100
But I can handle this and get it done

47
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:11,300
if you can promise me
Inspector Phat won’t get in the way again.

48
00:06:07,350 --> 00:06:09,600
The doctor said
you can go home now, Praew.

49
00:06:10,690 --> 00:06:12,200
Kaye and I are here to take you home.

50
00:06:14,210 --> 00:06:16,700
You want me to go home
and get on with my life

51
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,300
when my friend is still here like this?

52
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,100
Praew.

53
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,800
I understand what you’ve been through.

54
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:30,100
But it’s over now.

55
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:32,700
Piaw is dead.

56
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:35,600
Yeah, he did.

57
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,800
No freaking thanks to the police.

58
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:44,800
Don’t you think it’s funny that
while that asshole was hurting my friend,

59
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,800
all I could do was lie there?

60
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,250
And the person who saved me

61
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:54,500
wasn’t even a cop.

62
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:58,600
An asshole like you…

63
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:01,650
deserves to die.

64
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:12,400
That day
I wasn’t afraid of Nekros at all.

65
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:13,700
Praew.

66
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,940
He’s a murderer.

67
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:18,840
But that scumbag deserved his end
and you know it.

68
00:07:19,850 --> 00:07:21,730
Do you want to live in a world
where what is wrong or right

69
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:24,100
is decided by how you feel
and what you believe in?

70
00:07:24,530 --> 00:07:26,100
Vigilante punishment.

71
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:27,810
No laws.

72
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,400
Just death sentences without judgement.

73
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:35,210
Do you really want that?

74
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:38,250
But laws are useless against these scums!

75
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:41,290
If it wasn’t for Nekros,
you’d have found Prim and me as corpses.

76
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,300
You know what?

77
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:49,170
Someone who’s never been a victim like you
would never understand.

78
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:11,700
Yes, Uncle?

79
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:17,500
(I just got news that Kitti
was on to your scheme and has escaped.)

80
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,300
But what tipped him off?

81
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,100
Let’s not worry about that.

82
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:26,050
I’ll have him hunted down.

83
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:28,000
Phat.

84
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:30,700
You need to be careful from now on.

85
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:33,590
Talk to me before you take any actions.

86
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:35,200
Do you understand?

87
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:36,700
(Yes, Uncle.)

88
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:51,700
Someone tipped Kitti off about the arrest.

89
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,200
He caught on before he got booked.

90
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:57,100
Phat.

91
00:08:57,670 --> 00:09:00,700
You know what they did to Nop.

92
00:09:02,090 --> 00:09:03,900
If you keep on pushing like this,

93
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:06,700
I fear you’d be their next kill.

94
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,900
Do you want Nop to die for nothing?

95
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:16,600
Listen, Kaye.

96
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:21,000
I don’t care what big shot
is behind Kitti,

97
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:24,000
I’m dragging his ass out into the light.

98
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,000
Did the doctor take your mouth?

99
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:09,900
Come on.

100
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:12,700
Smile for me.

101
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:25,700
Kaye said he’d love to buy you
dinner some time.

102
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,460
You’re living the dream, huh?

103
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:28,670
Having dinner with your idol—

104
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:30,500
I’m going back to my internship tomorrow.

105
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:36,300
Praew.

106
00:10:37,290 --> 00:10:38,700
You’re just out of the hospital.

107
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,610
Don’t you think you should take a rest?

108
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:43,760
I know my strength better than anyone.

109
00:10:43,970 --> 00:10:45,250
Come on, Phat.

110
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:47,600
Don’t force your sister.

111
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,900
Praew isn’t a kid anymore.

112
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:52,900
Am I right, you troublemaker?

113
00:11:44,650 --> 00:11:45,700
Hello.

114
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:48,640
Yes.

115
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:50,700
I’ll submit it by the end of the day.

116
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,100
Excuse me.

117
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:13,300
I can pay for only one month right now…

118
00:12:14,230 --> 00:12:15,000
Of course.

119
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:18,700
But if this becomes a three-month overdue,
your father has to move.

120
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,100
Of course.

121
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,600
I’m sorry.

122
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:27,500
(Breaking News: There’s been a fire
at Pratum Thani’s Palliative Care Center.)

123
00:12:27,870 --> 00:12:29,800
(The fire was quickly out of control.)

124
00:12:30,190 --> 00:12:33,600
(Forensic physicians are working overtime
to identify the deceased,)

125
00:12:33,850 --> 00:12:39,400
(as many bodies are severely burned,
making it difficult for identification.)

126
00:12:40,350 --> 00:12:41,400
Thank you.

127
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,100
Please let me do it, Editor.

128
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,460
I don’t mind what you pay me.

129
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,000
I’m okay with it.

130
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,200
Alright.

131
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:38,300
Hello.

132
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,570
(We like your work.)

133
00:13:40,610 --> 00:13:42,260
(You can come in to collect your money.)

134
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,600
(I can give you 2000, excluding tax.)

135
00:13:47,230 --> 00:13:48,700
Thank you.

136
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:50,800
I’ll make sure I get it done tonight.

137
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,050
Even if you changed your name
and your address,

138
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:57,280
you won’t get away.

139
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:58,500
Remember this.

140
00:13:58,650 --> 00:14:01,460
Your dad may be dead,
but he still owes us money.

141
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,200
Dad, we have to run.

142
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:18,480
We’ll run so far they can’t find us.

143
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:52,700
Maybe…

144
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:55,100
The date of the first chapter publication?

145
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:56,800
It’s incorrect.

146
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:03,200
(Asura went to all this trouble
to lure youinto that abandoned building.)

147
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:06,730
His goal is for you to see
the ending he has planned.

148
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:09,450
(It has to be something you can guess.)

149
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:15,440
(And it must be something
only you and he know.)

150
00:17:39,090 --> 00:17:40,400
Welcome back.

151
00:17:40,770 --> 00:17:42,300
You have the perfect timing.

152
00:17:42,550 --> 00:17:44,900
I have something fun planned.

153
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,200
You’ll love it.

154
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:49,600
I know you’re more mature now, Praew.

155
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:53,700
You’re mature enough to understand that,
sometimes, to unearth the truth,

156
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:56,300
pain is necessary.

157
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:28,100
When did I fall asleep?

158
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:31,500
I saw you sleeping
so I didn’t want to wake you.

159
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:40,100
We have one chance left.

160
00:18:40,950 --> 00:18:42,100
Honestly,

161
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,610
I have no idea what the password could be.

162
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:50,700
What about Kitti?

163
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:57,600
This is my assumption.

164
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,290
Whoever is supporting Kitti

165
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:03,460
must be involved with the
Thai Investment Bank case 20 years ago.

166
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:05,800
It must be someone we have no idea about,

167
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:07,600
but Choti did.

168
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:11,100
So Kitti killed Choti to save this man?

169
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:14,100
He set up the murder scene
like Nekros did it,

170
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:16,900
and then framed me?

171
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:24,300
Yes.

172
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,000
The man Kitti serves

173
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:31,600
must be someone with enough power
to tamper with evidence.

174
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,100
If this falls apart,

175
00:19:44,630 --> 00:19:46,600
it’s not even the case
I’m most worried about.

176
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,330
What are you worried about then?

177
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:54,370
You.

178
00:19:59,090 --> 00:20:00,500
I’m worried you’d be targeted

179
00:20:01,350 --> 00:20:03,000
before we find out the truth.

180
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:12,540
(The Nekros case reveals more questions
than answers as it stretches out,)

181
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:15,790
(especially when connected
to Inspector Yotsaphat Traikanawut,)

182
00:20:15,830 --> 00:20:17,400
(the police officer initially
responsible for the case,)

183
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,680
(which reminds me of the saying)

184
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,600
(‘the apple doesn’t fall far
from the tree.’)

185
00:20:20,710 --> 00:20:23,000
(I can’t help but question)

186
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:26,250
(if the death of one
of the detectives on this case,)

187
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:28,320
(Lieutenant Nopphan Kongkram,)

188
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:32,300
(whose death was quietly decided
to be a robbery,)

189
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,700
(could hide something bigger.)

190
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:39,700
(Maybe the only person who has an answer
is Inspector Yotsaphat himself.)

191
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:42,000
Who the hell gave him
this kind of information?

192
00:20:42,310 --> 00:20:44,100
I did.

193
00:20:50,610 --> 00:20:51,400
Praew.

194
00:20:52,390 --> 00:20:53,700
He’s using you again.

195
00:20:54,570 --> 00:20:57,600
He’s just connecting dots
that aren’t there for some rating.

196
00:20:57,990 --> 00:20:59,100
I’m gonna ask you honestly.

197
00:20:59,870 --> 00:21:04,400
Are you really okay he keeps publicly
shaming our dad’s name?

198
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:06,500
No one is using me.

199
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:09,200
And what he said about Dad is true.

200
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:13,700
Even if Thun didn’t say anything,
we couldn’t change what Dad did.

201
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:17,100
And you know why I agreed to this?

202
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,800
Because if your name
wasn’t in the spotlight,

203
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:22,320
you’d be killed like Nop was.

204
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:29,800
Actually… Praew has a point.

205
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:45,000
We have a lead on Kitti.

206
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,100
I have to go.

207
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:49,000
Take care of Praew for me.

208
00:21:49,910 --> 00:21:50,700
Yeah.

209
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:58,600
I…

210
00:21:59,230 --> 00:22:00,400
I understand you, Praew.

211
00:22:00,770 --> 00:22:04,300
You did what you did
because you want to protect Phat.

212
00:22:07,450 --> 00:22:09,600
But someone who thinks himself
a protector like him

213
00:22:09,750 --> 00:22:10,970
would never understand.

214
00:22:14,230 --> 00:22:17,250
Thun told me he gave you
all the chapters of Nekros.

215
00:22:17,930 --> 00:22:19,000
Yes.

216
00:22:19,390 --> 00:22:21,300
Thun was a Nekros fan.

217
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:24,300
That's why he downloaded all the chapters.

218
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:26,400
But Praew…

219
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:32,500
I actually don’t think
Thun is just a regular fan.

220
00:22:34,810 --> 00:22:37,000
Are you suggesting Thun is Asura?

221
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:39,900
It’s possible.

222
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,601
I think this has gotten out of hand.

223
00:22:44,564 --> 00:22:46,300
It’s obvious someone has him killed.

224
00:22:47,386 --> 00:22:50,102
I’ll take care of the Kitti case myself,

225
00:22:51,210 --> 00:22:54,127
but both you and I have to withdraw
from the Nekros case.

226
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:59,300
Because it’s now involved with
the Thai Investment Bank.

227
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:02,900
If we got involved,
it’d be against Article 157.

228
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:05,845
We’d be condemned for having something
to gain from the case.

229
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:08,096
What about Nop?

230
00:23:09,510 --> 00:23:10,294
Phat.

231
00:23:11,555 --> 00:23:13,299
Do you still have faith in me?

232
00:23:14,437 --> 00:23:19,200
If you do, you must know a cop like me
will bring criminals to justice.

233
00:23:22,494 --> 00:23:23,930
Or have you lost your faith?

234
00:23:26,823 --> 00:23:29,902
Have you strayed into the way
of the devil like Nekros?

235
00:25:13,213 --> 00:25:14,102
What is it?

236
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:18,245
Praew texted me the link
to Thun’s live broadcast.

237
00:25:20,668 --> 00:25:21,897
(Hello, all.)

238
00:25:22,142 --> 00:25:26,330
(I am not here to reveal some secrets
or give you an update on anything.)

239
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:30,294
(But I am here to communicate
with Mr. Kill directly.)

240
00:25:31,351 --> 00:25:33,459
(I understand how you feel, Mr. Kill.)

241
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:36,400
(I understand how it feels
to watch the bad guys walk free.)

242
00:25:36,734 --> 00:25:40,300
(I understand the pain that
made you create a monster like Nekros.)

243
00:25:41,230 --> 00:25:43,300
(I don’t know if you’re watching,)

244
00:25:43,903 --> 00:25:47,000
(but let me be the one to beg you
in place of all your fans…)

245
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:51,080
(Everyone is waiting for
the perfect ending of Nekros.)

246
00:25:51,577 --> 00:25:57,290
(And if I were to guess, maybe the ending
is right where it all began.)

247
00:25:57,620 --> 00:25:59,930
(Am I right, dai-sensei?)

248
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:12,998
Phat.

249
00:26:13,376 --> 00:26:14,600
The term ‘dai-sensei.’

250
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:17,297
What? What about it?

251
00:26:17,736 --> 00:26:24,299
‘Dai-sensei’ is the term
Asura calls Mr. Kill in the inbox.

252
00:26:24,865 --> 00:26:26,410
It could be a coincidence.

253
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,200
I don’t think so.

254
00:26:28,911 --> 00:26:31,700
To call Mr. Kill ‘dai-sensei’
on live broadcast,

255
00:26:32,074 --> 00:26:33,998
he wants to send a message to Mr. Kill.

256
00:26:34,765 --> 00:26:37,000
If Thun really is Asura,

257
00:26:37,459 --> 00:26:40,397
revealing himself
on national television like this

258
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,650
means he’s up to something.

259
00:26:45,185 --> 00:26:47,700
Right now, Praew is with him.

260
00:26:49,416 --> 00:26:50,795
Praew could be in danger.

261
00:27:21,230 --> 00:27:22,245
Sir, please wait.

262
00:27:22,714 --> 00:27:24,120
What business do you have here?

263
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:24,949
Sir.

264
00:27:25,670 --> 00:27:26,602
Wait up.

265
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:34,299
Oh, Mr. Kaye. Inspector.

266
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:37,200
Are you here to see me…

267
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:40,201
Oh, maybe you’re here to see Praew?

268
00:27:42,328 --> 00:27:43,404
What’s the matter?

269
00:27:45,180 --> 00:27:46,800
You called me dai-sensei.

270
00:27:47,487 --> 00:27:49,600
Only one person in the world
calls me that.

271
00:27:50,398 --> 00:27:52,201
What’s strange about that?

272
00:27:52,936 --> 00:27:55,404
I’m a big fan of your work.

273
00:27:55,948 --> 00:28:00,897
I don’t think there’s another word
befitting my respect for you as a fan.

274
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:10,250
I know what you’re thinking.

275
00:28:11,048 --> 00:28:13,800
But I think there’s been
a misunderstanding about Thun.

276
00:28:14,441 --> 00:28:15,351
And you, Phat.

277
00:28:15,386 --> 00:28:16,903
As a cop, you should know…

278
00:28:17,838 --> 00:28:19,330
this is no evidence.

279
00:28:32,130 --> 00:28:33,200
I think we should go.

280
00:28:35,111 --> 00:28:37,296
Sorry for intruding.

281
00:28:44,437 --> 00:28:47,899
I’m pretty sure Thun has something to do
with the Thai Investment Back case.

282
00:28:49,105 --> 00:28:52,899
There’s no other reason
why he won’t let this case go.

283
00:28:57,309 --> 00:28:58,400
It’s possible.

284
00:29:05,820 --> 00:29:06,699
Found it.

285
00:29:07,770 --> 00:29:09,902
Thunwikorn Putthanan.

286
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:12,198
His parents were real estate agents

287
00:29:13,031 --> 00:29:16,099
who got swindled
by the Thai Investment Bank.

288
00:29:17,337 --> 00:29:21,297
They ended their own lives
to escape their debts.

289
00:29:25,325 --> 00:29:26,198
Dad!

290
00:29:37,327 --> 00:29:38,300
Which means…

291
00:29:38,850 --> 00:29:42,097
Thun isn’t just a sensationalist reporter
jumping along on the Nekros hype.

292
00:29:44,710 --> 00:29:47,696
If he really was the murderer,

293
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:50,897
this could be his motivation.

294
00:29:52,590 --> 00:29:54,597
His life isn’t all that different from mine.

295
00:30:07,915 --> 00:30:08,699
Well…

296
00:30:10,528 --> 00:30:11,602
I’m going home.

297
00:30:14,336 --> 00:30:15,457
Hey, Kaye.

298
00:30:18,291 --> 00:30:19,096
Kaye.

299
00:30:54,782 --> 00:30:55,804
Hello, Aunt Sri.

300
00:31:22,900 --> 00:31:23,697
Kaye.

301
00:31:23,990 --> 00:31:25,797
Kaye, it’s your father.

302
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:27,299
Come.

303
00:31:28,350 --> 00:31:29,776
It’s your father.

304
00:31:37,423 --> 00:31:39,195
Should we call an ambulance?

305
00:31:46,410 --> 00:31:47,700
It’s okay, Dad.

306
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:50,897
It’s okay…

307
00:33:10,216 --> 00:33:11,798
Uncle, why didn’t you tell me?

308
00:33:13,952 --> 00:33:16,930
You were one of the investigators
on the Thai Investment Bank case.

309
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:24,850
COURT MARSHAL
INSPECTOR CHAIWAT TRAIKANAWUT

310
00:33:25,230 --> 00:33:26,097
Yes.

311
00:33:26,647 --> 00:33:29,997
It was true I was involved in
the Thai Investment Bank case.

312
00:33:32,284 --> 00:33:34,002
But I wasn’t the main investigator.

313
00:33:36,940 --> 00:33:39,200
Why didn’t you tell me?

314
00:33:42,287 --> 00:33:44,697
Nekros is targeting you.

315
00:33:45,114 --> 00:33:48,801
And those journalists are gonna
drag you into the spotlight.

316
00:33:52,237 --> 00:33:54,100
I’ll have my men keep you safe.

317
00:33:54,325 --> 00:33:55,302
No.

318
00:33:55,690 --> 00:33:57,902
I won’t push back against this.

319
00:33:59,124 --> 00:34:01,302
And I don’t need protection.

320
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:08,097
If I do, it means what those reporters
are digging up and trying to frame me for…

321
00:34:09,161 --> 00:34:10,400
is true.

322
00:34:14,570 --> 00:34:15,699
You do know

323
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:21,800
how every victim who said that
met their end?

324
00:34:28,306 --> 00:34:29,602
Don’t worry about me.

325
00:34:30,645 --> 00:34:33,998
My house has a top-notch security system.

326
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:41,899
You know if Nekros can’t do anything,
everything will have been a lie.

327
00:34:42,251 --> 00:34:44,398
And I won’t even have
to make excuses for myself.

328
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:45,896
Am I right?

329
00:36:01,205 --> 00:36:05,103
(…maybe the ending is right
where it all began.)

330
00:36:06,210 --> 00:36:08,200
(Am I right, dai-sensei?)

331
00:36:11,700 --> 00:36:13,900
(Right where it all began.)

332
00:36:15,253 --> 00:36:18,010
(Right where it all began.)

333
00:36:18,040 --> 00:36:19,998
CASE A045678

334
00:36:20,042 --> 00:36:21,998
(Am I right, dai-sensei?)

335
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:58,170
PHAT
INCOMING CALL

336
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:10,441
Kaye.

337
00:37:15,468 --> 00:37:16,705
Damn it.

338
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:19,250
Kaye!

339
00:37:20,470 --> 00:37:21,401
Hey, Kaye!

340
00:37:26,965 --> 00:37:27,702
Kaye.

341
00:37:39,245 --> 00:37:42,900
It seems Mr. Kill has heard the plea
from me and his fans.

342
00:37:43,250 --> 00:37:47,202
The ending of Nekros
was just uploaded minutes ago.

343
00:37:57,017 --> 00:38:00,899
(And of course,
it brings us bigger questions.)

344
00:38:01,114 --> 00:38:05,530
(Because the worst thing in the world
isn’t crimes committed by bad people,)

345
00:38:05,764 --> 00:38:09,890
but the dishonesty from the people
who are supposed to be on justice’s side.

346
00:38:10,491 --> 00:38:13,204
It is the perfect ending.

347
00:38:20,628 --> 00:38:23,697
I don’t know who Nekros is pointing at.

348
00:38:24,190 --> 00:38:27,880
But I can say for sure
that the worst thing is

349
00:38:28,665 --> 00:38:32,200
when law enforcers themselves
are the bad guys.

350
00:38:32,831 --> 00:38:34,899
Who would we turn to if that was the case?

351
00:39:12,149 --> 00:39:13,097
Hey, Kaye.

352
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:26,099
Just listen to me.

353
00:39:27,865 --> 00:39:30,760
You really think this will be over
just because you did this?

354
00:39:31,614 --> 00:39:34,598
In the end, you’re just a tool…

355
00:39:35,168 --> 00:39:36,600
(for Thun to use.)

356
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:41,330
I know this isn’t what you want.

357
00:39:44,334 --> 00:39:45,198
Why are you quiet?

358
00:39:45,758 --> 00:39:46,600
Talk to me!

359
00:39:48,158 --> 00:39:49,202
(I’m sorry.)

360
00:39:52,068 --> 00:39:52,802
Kaye.

361
00:39:53,306 --> 00:39:54,496
Kaye! Kaye!

362
00:39:55,294 --> 00:39:56,202
Shit!

363
00:41:00,761 --> 00:41:01,804
Hello, Inspector.

364
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:04,601
Is anything out of the ordinary?

365
00:41:04,834 --> 00:41:05,810
Everything is fine, sir.

366
00:41:06,808 --> 00:41:11,801
Oh, your sister came over
to visit your uncle about an hour ago.

367
00:41:12,030 --> 00:41:13,195
She left, though.

368
00:41:15,927 --> 00:41:16,699
Thank you.

369
00:41:27,635 --> 00:41:28,401
Uncle.

370
00:41:32,992 --> 00:41:33,798
Uncle.

371
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:53,730
UNCLE CHAIWAT

372
00:42:02,429 --> 00:42:06,200
(Oh, your sister came over
to visit your uncle about an hour ago.)

373
00:42:07,325 --> 00:42:10,210
If it wasn’t for Nekros,
you’d have found Prim and me as corpses.

374
00:42:11,671 --> 00:42:13,450
(His parents were real estate agents)

375
00:42:13,485 --> 00:42:16,496
(who got swindled
by the Thai Investment Bank.)

376
00:42:16,737 --> 00:42:18,757
(They ended their own lives…)

377
00:42:18,813 --> 00:42:20,300
So Thun is another victim.

378
00:42:20,471 --> 00:42:23,290
Someone who’s never been a victim like you
would never understand.

379
00:42:23,390 --> 00:42:27,456
(There’s a type of murderer
called a mastermind.)

380
00:42:28,380 --> 00:42:30,299
(He wouldn’t get his hands bloodied.)

381
00:42:30,497 --> 00:42:32,300
(He borrows someone else’s hands
to do his dirty work.)

382
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:41,320
PRAEW

383
00:43:40,715 --> 00:43:42,499
If I didn’t get Nop involved,

384
00:43:45,988 --> 00:43:47,699
he wouldn’t have died.

385
00:43:49,288 --> 00:43:50,173
Would he?

386
00:43:57,370 --> 00:43:59,460
He wouldn’t have died…

387
00:44:30,482 --> 00:44:32,170
Now that you know the whole truth,

388
00:44:32,361 --> 00:44:36,195
how do you think all this crap
should end, Praew?

389
00:44:36,834 --> 00:44:38,696
Take this story to the end.

390
00:44:39,322 --> 00:44:40,970
If you don’t stop them now,

391
00:44:41,207 --> 00:44:43,490
Praew will become a murderer
just like Kim did.

392
00:44:44,260 --> 00:44:46,001
Will you promise me one thing?

393
00:44:46,545 --> 00:44:48,810
Promise me you will protect the innocent.

394
00:44:49,074 --> 00:44:51,454
Promise me you won’t let anyone
go through what I did.

395
00:44:52,042 --> 00:44:52,997
I promise.
